.TH BTRFS-BACKUP 8 "September 2026" "btrfs-backup 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
btrfs-backup \- run an encrypted removable Btrfs backup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B btrfs-backup
.RB [ --profile " " ID ]
.RB [ --force ]
.RB [ --validate ]
.RB [ --no-eject ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B btrfs-backup
runs the configured backup profile. It validates and mounts the exact LUKS2
target, creates read-only source snapshots, transfers them with Btrfs
send/receive, applies retention and optionally ejects the target.
.PP
Automatic runs are normally started by the installed udev and systemd units.
The command is also suitable for a manual run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --profile " ID"
Use the named profile. The default is
.BR default .
.TP
.B --force
Run even when the profile has already completed successfully today.
.TP
.B --validate
Mount and validate the target and configuration without creating snapshots.
.TP
.B --no-eject
Leave the target mounted after a manual invocation.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Show the program version.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show command help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/btrfs-backup/profiles/ID/profile.json
Canonical profile configuration.
.TP
.I /run/btrfs-backup/profiles
Current status and cancellation state.
.TP
.I /var/lib/btrfs-backup
Persistent history and recovery state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR btrfs-backupctl (1),
.BR btrfs (8),
.BR cryptsetup (8),
.BR systemd (1)
